Most if not all of our apps use monday.com app settings or board item columns to store data such as URLs for embedding external URLs. As such, we cannot sanitise the data stored in monday.com (even though monday.com will do some of this).

We do however ensure that all data is sanitised before accepting it’s use in our apps.

An example of this is the URL checking logic:

```
const isUrl = (url) => {
  try {
    new URL(url); // trigger catch exception for invalid URLs 
    return true;
  } catch (e) {
    return false;
  }
};
```

