We use React, which has built-in XSS protection.
We are using library to sanitize our input as you can see here is how we handle URLs.
import { sanitizeUrl } from "@braintree/sanitize-url";
...
sanitizeUrl(link);

We also have linting checks to notify the unsafe coding patterns.

The project has DOMpurify-er installed.

import DOMPurify from 'dompurify';

Text is sanitized before being sent to monday's API (that further handles it based on our tests and docs):

const sanitizedText = DOMPurify.sanitize(notificationText); let htmlNotificationText = marked(sanitizedText);
htmlNotificationText = htmlNotificationText.replace(/"/g, "'");
const notificationPromises = notifyUsers.map((userId) => sendNotification(userId, htmlNotificationText, boardId), );

import { sanitize } from 'sanitize-html';
app.use((req: Request, res: Response, next: NextFunction) => {
  req.body = sanitize(req.body);
  next();
});

